    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19519" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gerres</span></b> , is, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an inferior salted
				seafish</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 32, 11, 53, § 148</span></i>
			Sill. (al. girres), <i><span class="en">Mart. 12, 32, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 77, 7</span></i>; cf.: gerres
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαινίδες</span>, Gloss.
			Philox.—Prov.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">addere garo gerrem,</span>”
				i. e. <i>to add to what is precious something
					worthless</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 5, 188</span></i>
			.</div>
